1
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:48,000
<i>When does the competition of life</i>
<i>really begin?</i>

3
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:54,440
<i>Is it when your parents finally beat</i>
<i>all odds to be together?</i>

4
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:58,720
<i>Or when that specific sperm and egg,</i>

5
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:01,800
<i>out of billions, found each other?</i>

6
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:05,720
<i>Then you fight, you grow,</i>
<i>follow the set path,</i>

7
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:09,360
<i>and step into a whole new battlefield.</i>

8
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:11,400
<i>You struggle with money and feelings,</i>

9
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:12,440
<i>go through countless suffering,</i>

10
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:15,200
<i>and finally get to show a happy smile.</i>

11
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:16,200
<i>But even then,</i>

12
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:17,120
‎BEICHEN UNIVERSITY
‎COMMENCEMENT CEREMONY

13
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:18,720
<i>you can't afford to let your guard down</i>

14
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,720
<i>because you're afraid of failing.</i>

15
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:24,640
<i>Even more afraid of being replaced</i>
<i>someday, without warning.</i>

16
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:27,760
WHAT'S THE BIGGEST CHALLENGE
YOU'VE EVER FACED?

17
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:29,040
<i>My parents divorced.</i>

18
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:31,240
<i>Since high school, I've been on my own.</i>

19
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,880
I have no family to back me up,

20
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:36,840
but I'm not afraid of that challenge.

21
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:39,760
Because compared
to the tough job market ahead,

22
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:41,640
it's nothing.

23
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:42,840
It's a good story.

24
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:48,200
YE XINZHI, OPERATIONS DIRECTOR AT P&amp;J

25
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:50,360
P&amp;J INTERNSHIP PROGRAM, SECOND INTERVIEW

26
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:52,480
Thank you.

27
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:57,200
Every story comes from life.

28
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,760
Actually, your founder, Mr. Pang Li,

29
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:05,480
said at the APEC summit in July 2006

30
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:09,600
that storytelling and courage
are the foundations of success.

31
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:11,760
It's because of those words
that I dared to compete

32
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:13,240
for this interview invitation,

33
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:15,200
which used to be
only for second-year grad students,

34
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:16,120
during my first-year break.

35
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:19,120
When faced with doubt, agree first,

36
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:20,680
then smoothly steer to another topic.

37
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:23,880
Textbook stiff.

38
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:26,600
-I--
-Next question.

39
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:31,200
What's your life motto?

40
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:45,640
Always work hard,

41
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:50,880
and never, ever become someone

42
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,800
who can be easily replaced.

43
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,240
Really?

44
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,840
Are you that afraid of being replaced?

45
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:02,960
Next.

46
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:05,800
If I get this internship offer from P&amp;J,

47
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:07,240
my job will be locked in
when I graduate next year.

48
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:08,400
I'm telling you,

49
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:10,600
that Mr. Ye, who interviewed me
last time, is really hot.

50
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:11,960
Totally. I remember him clearly too.

51
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:12,880
‎Hey…

52
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:15,320
With so many people at the interview,

53
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,440
I don't feel confident about it.

54
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:20,480
Chi.

55
00:04:21,279 --> 00:04:22,320
You just got here?

56
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:24,560
Morning. Got stuck in traffic.

57
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,080
You look down.

58
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:28,120
You're definitely not getting in.

59
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:30,560
-What are you saying?
-How do you know I won't make it?

60
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:32,280
I'm telling you,

61
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:33,960
I'm getting into P&amp;J now,

62
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:36,400
and later, I'm getting
into Maxmise and Boen.

63
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:38,680
Are you kidding me?

64
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:41,480
Top consulting firms like those
only hire from top schools.

65
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:46,160
Those who are incompetent
always treat "always" and "usually"

66
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:47,840
as unbreakable ceilings.

67
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:50,040
Alright. Stop it.

68
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:53,200
-The interview results are out! Come!
-Results are out!

69
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:54,880
I'll go check for you.

70
00:04:56,440 --> 00:04:57,440
Excuse me. Coming through.

71
00:04:57,520 --> 00:04:58,520
Sorry.

72
00:04:58,600 --> 00:04:59,520
‎Wait.

73
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:01,120
NAME, GENDER

74
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:08,560
XU CHI

75
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:09,320
NOT ADMITTED

76
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:10,040
What?

77
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:11,280
Look.

78
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:13,080
-Neither of us made it.
-You didn't make it.

79
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:25,360
Scared to look?

80
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:28,400
Congratulations.

81
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:31,000
Ch… Chi.

82
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:32,960
I read the wrong line. You got in.

83
00:05:36,960 --> 00:05:37,800
Thank you.

84
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:43,120
Weren't you pretty confident?

85
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:44,520
Why did you chicken out?

86
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:48,480
I didn't.

87
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:51,600
I just didn't believe I'd fail.

88
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:54,680
Big talk.

89
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:57,440
You're good enough
for a consumer goods company

90
00:05:57,520 --> 00:05:58,520
like P&amp;J,

91
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:02,640
but for consulting firms,
you still fall short.

92
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:04,680
How did you know I wanted to get into--?

93
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:06,200
Why do you want to get
into Boen and Maxmise?

94
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:10,840
Because, much like P&amp;J,
they are all top players in the industry.

95
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:13,000
Since I was little, I've had a dream.

96
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:15,080
I wanted to be the best management talent.

97
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:17,440
Stop reciting from AI scripts.

98
00:06:20,240 --> 00:06:23,280
I've always been passionate
about international work experience.

99
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:24,600
-Stop.
-I--

100
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:27,280
Next time, just talk like a real person.

101
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:29,080
I want money!

102
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:48,280
NO. 92, YONG'AN ROAD

103
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:52,920
I just want money.

104
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:58,040
What I just told you wasn't a story.
It's all true.

105
00:06:58,120 --> 00:06:59,560
My mom killed herself.

106
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:01,520
My dad married the other woman
and had a son.

107
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:04,800
I even had to borrow living expenses
from my high school homeroom teacher.

108
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:06,960
So I need money. A lot of it.

109
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:08,560
I need to pay back what I owe.

110
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:10,720
And I need to go work in Beijing.

111
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:13,960
I want to buy back the old apartment
my mom couldn't let go of.

112
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,880
But I picked the wrong major.

113
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:17,120
As my bachelor's graduation
drew near, I figured

114
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:18,080
I couldn't land jobs
at major internet companies

115
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:19,120
or make it into investment banking.

116
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:20,760
After grad school,

117
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:22,080
my advisor ran
a career-profile assessment on me

118
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:23,520
and said I was suited
for management consulting.

119
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:26,080
Consulting firms also pay pretty well
for fresh grads.

120
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:27,600
But my school isn't prestigious.

121
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:29,280
My senior told me
I could start as a summer intern

122
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:30,560
at a Fortune 500 company first.

123
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:31,720
Once I have experience,

124
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:33,440
I can get an internship
at a consulting firm.

125
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:36,960
Top consulting firms
haven't been hiring much lately.

126
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,920
And they still keep
that insane elimination rate.

127
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,360
A third of people get cut every year.

128
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:44,360
Sixty percent of new hires
leave within the first year.

129
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:46,480
You sure you can last three years?

130
00:07:48,720 --> 00:07:51,720
I'm sure.
I will never be replaced by anyone.

131
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:56,720
I'll be the one to push out
those competing with me first.

132
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:04,880
Then don't go to Maxmise.

133
00:08:04,960 --> 00:08:07,160
They won't hire someone
from a non-elite school like yours.

134
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:08,880
Go to Beisen instead.

135
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:10,480
Their campus recruitment is more open.

136
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:13,000
If you win an award
at Beisen's Yangfan Cup,

137
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:14,880
you get direct access
to the final interview.

138
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:16,760
One more piece of advice.

139
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:18,880
Raise your GPA,
learn logical methodology well,

140
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:20,240
and read The Pyramid Principle.

141
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:22,560
By the way, drop the name Tracy.

142
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:24,200
In consulting circles,
there are 50 Vivians,

143
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:26,240
a hundred Lisas, and 200 Alexes.

144
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:28,280
Don't you want to avoid being replaced?

145
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:31,040
Then make people remember
your uniqueness from the very start.

146
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:32,679
Your name is Xu Chi.

147
00:08:32,760 --> 00:08:33,919
It's already quite nice.

148
00:08:34,520 --> 00:08:36,000
As in "A gentle breeze comes,
the sentiments linger."

149
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:38,000
Good luck.

150
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:03,240
<i>In this world,</i>

151
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,840
<i>there's always someone</i>
<i>who gives you a gentle push</i>

152
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:06,280
<i>when you're lost.</i>

153
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:08,200
<i>Every word Ye Xinzhi said</i>

154
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:10,320
<i>was like a precise coordinate,</i>

155
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:13,040
<i>helping me find direction</i>
<i>in the chaos ahead.</i>

156
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:16,440
<i>So I dove straight into the YangFan Cup.</i>

157
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:18,320
<i>With that never-give-up attitude,</i>

158
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:21,600
<i>I landed an offer</i>
<i>from the top consulting firm Beisen.</i>

159
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:25,920
<i>And Ye Xinzhi and I</i>
<i>were like two parallel lines.</i>

160
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,600
<i>After all the twists and turns,</i>

161
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:31,400
<i>who knows when our paths</i>

162
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:32,960
<i>would cross again.</i>

163
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:39,720
‎BEIJING

164
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:42,800
Miss, are you looking at properties?

165
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:46,560
Is the one with the flowers
on the second floor for sale?

166
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:48,280
That one? It's not on the market.

167
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:51,040
Alright. Let me know
if you need anything. Bye.

168
00:09:54,040 --> 00:09:58,560
NO. 92, YONG'AN ROAD

169
00:09:58,640 --> 00:10:00,480
This isn't the first time!

170
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:02,800
NAME: CHENGYA

171
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:12,840
Chi.

172
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:15,400
Your dad doesn't want us anymore.

173
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:19,400
He found someone younger and prettier.

174
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:22,240
He's such a scumbag!

175
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:24,600
‎Mom.

176
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:32,520
<i>Chi. I'm sorry.</i>

177
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:35,320
<i>I didn't mean to abandon you.</i>

178
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:38,400
<i>It's just that living hurts too much.</i>

179
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:41,400
<i>I gave so much for your dad.</i>

180
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:44,200
<i>I even sold the apartment</i>
<i>in Beijing your grandma left me</i>

181
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:46,280
<i>to fund his business.</i>

182
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:49,400
<i>But he still found another woman.</i>

183
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:51,640
<i>You must remember,</i>

184
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:54,720
<i>even on your own,</i>
<i>you still have to work hard</i>

185
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:56,080
-Dad!
-<i>and keep striving.</i>

186
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:59,040
-Dad!
-<i>Don't end up useless like me,</i>

187
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:02,600
-<i>someone who can be easily replaced.</i>
-Dad!

188
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:04,120
<i>Chi.</i>

189
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:06,800
<i>I regret it so much.</i>

190
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:10,040
<i>If we hadn't sold that apartment,</i>

191
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:12,440
<i>we'd still have a home to go back to,</i>

192
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:16,800
<i>and I could've watched the flowers</i>
<i>on the windowsill bloom,</i>

193
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:21,360
<i>and you grow up just like before.</i>

194
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,720
YONG'AN ROAD COMMUNITY
3-BEDROOM, 4.5 MILLION

195
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:26,720
<i>Mom. I've already got an offer</i>
<i>from a Beijing consulting firm now.</i>

196
00:11:26,800 --> 00:11:28,320
<i>Just wait a little longer.</i>

197
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:30,840
<i>I will buy back our old apartment.</i>

198
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:34,760
Heard this year's orientation

199
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:37,560
is being run by Samantha,
who's about to be made a junior partner.

200
00:11:37,640 --> 00:11:39,840
Right now, Maxmise North China
has two partners in total.

201
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:40,800
One is Mr. Pi, the other is Mr. Li.

202
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:43,000
Samantha is Mr. Pi's right-hand woman.

203
00:11:44,320 --> 00:11:47,160
Xu… Chi.

204
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:48,920
Why is this in pinyin?

205
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,080
How do you say that?

206
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:53,400
You don't even have an English name?

207
00:11:58,480 --> 00:11:59,520
Xu Chi.

208
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:01,800
As in "A gentle breeze comes,
the sentiments linger."

209
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:03,360
I think my name sounds pretty good,
so I kept it.

210
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:07,240
Xu Chi? I think it sounds good too.

211
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:09,200
Besides, we're all Chinese.

212
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:11,480
Working at a company in China,
using an English name

213
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:13,920
always feels a bit off to me.

214
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:19,320
My name is Zhao Heng.

215
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:21,600
Heng as in "eternal".

216
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:22,800
Emperor Zhenzong of Song?

217
00:12:23,760 --> 00:12:24,960
You actually know that.

218
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:28,760
My dad thought it was cool
because an emperor used it,

219
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:29,680
but then he worried
I couldn't live up to it.

220
00:12:29,760 --> 00:12:30,600
I think I can't either.

221
00:12:31,760 --> 00:12:33,600
So I changed it to Ben.

222
00:12:33,680 --> 00:12:35,440
What's Ben? As in "dumb"!

223
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:38,480
You're actually really good at dad jokes.

224
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,040
Oh right.

225
00:12:43,120 --> 00:12:44,480
I'm a SJTU economics-management
graduate. What about you?

226
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:48,520
I'm in applied statistics.

227
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:50,920
Not answering directly?

228
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:53,320
Guess your school and name
aren't worth mentioning.

229
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:56,320
-Don't say that.
-What?

230
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:58,520
With this job market,

231
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:01,000
even Maxmise cut
10% of their senior staff.

232
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:03,280
With consulting's high elimination rate,

233
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:05,160
half of us will be gone in the first year.

234
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:07,400
Since we're bound to compete anyway,

235
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,880
why bother pretending to be all friendly?

236
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,880
You're pretty confident
in your abilities, huh?

237
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:21,240
Come here.

238
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:25,960
Yeah, you. Tall one.

239
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:34,880
Do you know the budget
for Maxmise's global partnership team?

240
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:41,040
Is she Samantha?

241
00:13:41,560 --> 00:13:42,960
Should be.

242
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:45,160
Can't answer?

243
00:13:46,880 --> 00:13:48,680
Two hundred million!

244
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:55,920
So, which prestigious school
did you graduate from?

245
00:13:59,280 --> 00:14:00,320
Cor…

246
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:02,760
Cor what?

247
00:14:05,160 --> 00:14:06,160
Cornell.

248
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,560
Thought it'd be HYPSM.

249
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:10,240
Turns out you just barely scraped an Ivy.

250
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:11,200
Who asked you?

251
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:15,520
Sorry. The meeting ran long.

252
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:17,200
I'm Sha Sha, Samantha,

253
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:18,920
head of this year's new hire orientation.

254
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,680
Have you all gotten to know each other?

255
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:27,080
Alright. Have a seat.

256
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:37,560
-Welcome to Maxmise.
-Thank you.

257
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:38,960
From now on,

258
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:41,280
your title is Business Analyst,

259
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:42,280
or BA for short.

260
00:14:42,360 --> 00:14:43,280
Business Analyst.

261
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:44,800
Throughout the internship,

262
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:46,800
each of you will join a team

263
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:49,520
and be assigned a senior mentor.

264
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:52,000
You'll also be their assistant.

265
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:55,720
<i>Maxmise gives you the best</i>
<i>and fairest opportunities for growth.</i>

266
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:57,960
Bu Tianna's scores
are practically perfect.

267
00:14:58,040 --> 00:14:58,880
If you're picking, go with her.

268
00:14:59,720 --> 00:15:01,920
Her internship record is truly top-tier.

269
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:05,560
Don't any of you fight me on this.

270
00:15:05,640 --> 00:15:08,360
I'm taking Bu Tianna.

271
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:10,960
Who would dare go against you?

272
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:13,000
But honey, not to nag,

273
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:16,560
you look terrible these days,
yet you’re still pushing yourself so hard.

274
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:19,360
Being a mentor is no easy job.

275
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:22,040
No choice. I've got a huge mortgage,

276
00:15:22,120 --> 00:15:24,280
and I've got
a little money pit on the way.

277
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:26,280
If I don't fight
to get a capable assistant,

278
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:27,400
my projects will get snatched away,

279
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:30,960
just like that Sato Pharmaceuticals deal.

280
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:34,000
Hon, that Sato Pharmaceulticals thing
really wasn't my fault.

281
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:36,280
Sha Sha wouldn't let you fly
because of your pregnancy risks,

282
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:37,640
so she had me take over midway.

283
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:39,560
I'm heading abroad the day after tomorrow.

284
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:41,400
I'll pick up some skincare
for you at duty-free.

285
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:44,960
Someone as easily annoyed as you
gets wrinkles fast.

286
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:48,080
Hurry up and choose.
We need to go in soon.

287
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:51,240
I'll take this guy, Zhao Heng.

288
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:53,880
Deng Anran.

289
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:56,400
Then I guess I'm stuck with Xu Chi.

290
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:01,280
BU TIANNA, TINA

291
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:04,320
<i>Under the guidance</i>
<i>of these mentors and seniors,</i>

292
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:06,360
you'll move forward step by step.

293
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:09,200
Everyone, please stand
and welcome your mentors.

294
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:19,800
-Welcome.
-Hello.

295
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:23,640
I saw you at the front desk earlier,
and I felt we were destined to meet.

296
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:25,240
HALF AN HOUR AGO

297
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:27,040
Hi, I'm Xu Chi. Here to check in.

298
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:28,760
Sure. Please follow me.

299
00:16:29,560 --> 00:16:31,720
Thanks, Ms. Lin. I'll do my best.

300
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:35,920
At Maxmise, we don't follow
the 9-to-9 six-day schedule,

301
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,440
and we won't force you to work overtime.

302
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:40,320
But you might have to get used
to running on little sleep from now on.

303
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,960
When I was interning in Seattle,

304
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,800
I only got six hours of sleep a day.

305
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:47,320
Right. We're here at Maxmise
to get tortured.

306
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:50,360
This. This is your desk.

307
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:52,480
Take a look.

308
00:16:55,320 --> 00:16:57,480
Among the new hires, you're pretty lucky.

309
00:16:57,560 --> 00:16:59,560
I put your desk right across from mine.

310
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:01,280
Makes it easier for us to communicate.

311
00:17:01,800 --> 00:17:03,320
-Thank you, Ms. Lin.
-Have a seat.

312
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:04,920
Get familiar with things.

313
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,319
Here's your computer
and the employee handbook.

314
00:17:16,839 --> 00:17:18,599
Why did you push her away?

315
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:20,119
Isn't that just handing her to Cindy?

316
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:22,839
Her full name is Bu Tianna.

317
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:23,760
BU TIANNA

318
00:17:23,839 --> 00:17:26,480
<i>Remember that Qianhai Bank project we did?</i>

319
00:17:26,560 --> 00:17:27,920
That's the name listed

320
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,280
as the beneficiary of Mr. Bu's
family trust at Siwei Group.

321
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:34,800
No wonder Mr. Pi
personally interviewed her.

322
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:36,480
She's the real deal.

323
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:38,120
Rich, well-connected, and capable.

324
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:39,680
If she got into my team,

325
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:41,200
by the time I come back
from maternity leave,

326
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:43,560
my projects
would just be stepping stones for her.

327
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:45,600
Might as well let Cindy taste

328
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:47,760
what it's like to work
for someone else's gain.

329
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:49,960
I've always worried

330
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:51,760
about being sidelined
because of all my time off.

331
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:53,640
Why would I want
a mentee who's that capable?

332
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:55,200
Makes sense.

333
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:57,880
Xu Chi does seem pretty steady.

334
00:17:57,960 --> 00:18:00,360
She got dissed like that
and still didn't snap back.

335
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:04,440
This girl doesn't fight or scheme.

336
00:18:04,520 --> 00:18:05,800
I actually like her.

337
00:18:05,880 --> 00:18:07,560
Sure. Please follow me.

338
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,200
Ms. Lin.

339
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:11,120
Thanks.

340
00:18:12,280 --> 00:18:13,800
Did you get her resume
during the interviews?

341
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:15,000
What's her background?

342
00:18:15,080 --> 00:18:16,280
I'm not sure.

343
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:18,160
I just remember
she doesn't have an overseas degree.

344
00:18:24,320 --> 00:18:25,800
As long as she follows my orders

345
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:27,640
while I'm on maternity leave,
that's all that matters.

346
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:29,880
Right. I'll get back to work then.

347
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:37,960
-How's it going?
-Ms. Lin,

348
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:40,200
you didn't look too well.

349
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:42,200
I read online that chocolate can help.

350
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:47,560
You're so sweet.

351
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:49,120
Have a seat.

352
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:50,680
-Did you read the employee handbook?
-I did.

353
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:53,240
It has your email
and your system username and password.

354
00:18:53,320 --> 00:18:54,840
-Got it.
-I'll send you the work plan

355
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:56,640
for the next few days later. Take a look.

356
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:58,720
If you don't understand anything,
feel free to ask me.

357
00:18:58,800 --> 00:19:00,080
Sure. No problem.

358
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,040
Our work is simple, in a way.

359
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:04,320
Start with data analysis.

360
00:19:04,400 --> 00:19:06,160
-Ever heard of Bolo Culture?
-Yes.

361
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:09,960
Pull Bolo Culture's data from the database
and do a basic analysis.

362
00:19:10,040 --> 00:19:11,240
No problem.

363
00:19:16,520 --> 00:19:17,360
Here's a tip.

364
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:19,760
Don't always say "yes" or "sure"
to everything when you're new.

365
00:19:19,840 --> 00:19:20,680
Sounds too much like a student.

366
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:21,920
In the workplace,

367
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:24,760
unless you're truly capable
of taking responsibility,

368
00:19:24,840 --> 00:19:26,920
don't just casually say "no problem".

369
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:32,600
Go on.

370
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:46,400
If you're not feeling well,
you should head home early.

371
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:47,600
If you collapse from exhaustion,

372
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:48,720
we'll have to call an ambulance for you.

373
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:49,760
That'll just hold everyone up.

374
00:19:50,360 --> 00:19:51,840
Relax. I can still hang on.

375
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:53,480
With you off to Japan,

376
00:19:53,560 --> 00:19:55,160
if something goes wrong here,

377
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:57,480
I'll have to clean up for you.

378
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:04,560
The report's done and sent to your email.

379
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:09,000
That fast?

380
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:11,760
I've been following
the online reading industry for a while.

381
00:20:11,840 --> 00:20:12,680
So…

382
00:20:12,760 --> 00:20:14,800
You want to prove yourself. I get it.

383
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:16,760
But honestly,
there's no need to rush like that.

384
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:20,320
Plus, Maxmise has its own
formatting rules for documents.

385
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:22,680
Not like the ones you did in school--

386
00:20:24,760 --> 00:20:25,800
CONTENTS

387
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:26,960
CONTENTS, EXECUTIVE SUMMARY

388
00:20:27,040 --> 00:20:28,520
PROJECT BACKGROUND
INTEGRATION CHALLENGES…

389
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:33,080
I did my homework.

390
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:35,120
Not bad.

391
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:37,800
But where did you get
all this data from Nielsu

392
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:39,120
and those business research firms?

393
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:41,120
I don't remember the company buying those.

394
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:42,480
I bought them myself.

395
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:47,720
But how could a student afford

396
00:20:47,800 --> 00:20:49,680
such expensive
business research databases?

397
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:52,200
If you want to get into Maxmise,

398
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:53,920
you have to pay some tuition yourself.

399
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,560
Being prepared is never wrong.

400
00:20:57,840 --> 00:20:59,320
Nice report.

401
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:00,880
I'll send you
the Yuanming project files later.

402
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:01,800
Keep doing the analysis.

403
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:03,120
Okay.

404
00:21:27,720 --> 00:21:28,640
Ma'am, your coffee.

405
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:29,800
Thank you.

406
00:21:36,800 --> 00:21:37,720
Sorry.

407
00:21:38,880 --> 00:21:40,560
-Thanks.
-No worries.

408
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:44,880
Actually, I've been watching you
for a while.

409
00:21:46,240 --> 00:21:48,800
Your folders are organized
like you have OCD.

410
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:51,680
All your files end with V1, V2, V3.

411
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:55,560
And those blue slide templates
with no images.

412
00:21:55,640 --> 00:21:57,600
Are you a consultant?

413
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:59,640
You're an executive at Beihuan Air, right?

414
00:22:00,680 --> 00:22:02,320
Public relations side?

415
00:22:02,400 --> 00:22:03,640
Yes.

416
00:22:03,720 --> 00:22:04,680
I'm heading to Beijing
for a headquarters meeting.

417
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:08,040
<i>Attention, all passengers.</i>

418
00:22:08,120 --> 00:22:10,760
<i>Flight to Beijing is now boarding.</i>

419
00:22:10,840 --> 00:22:12,400
-<i>Please prepare for boarding.</i>
-I need to board.

420
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:15,640
I'm on the next flight to Beijing.

421
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:18,000
After we land, do you want
to grab a drink sometime?

422
00:22:18,080 --> 00:22:19,200
Sorry.

423
00:22:19,280 --> 00:22:20,680
I've got work arrangements today.
Maybe some other time.

424
00:22:21,280 --> 00:22:23,600
Who knows when we'll run
into each other again.

425
00:22:23,680 --> 00:22:25,920
Soon. I have a feeling.

426
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:35,760
Thank you all for your contributions
to Beihuan Air over the years.

427
00:22:36,840 --> 00:22:38,080
HR will have one-on-one meetings

428
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:41,600
with everyone about
the specific compensation details later.

429
00:22:55,120 --> 00:22:57,720
Every business war has its casualties.

430
00:22:58,240 --> 00:22:59,280
A consultant's job

431
00:22:59,360 --> 00:23:02,200
is to secure the biggest win
with the smallest sacrifice

432
00:23:02,280 --> 00:23:04,960
and keep companies from going
into bankruptcy and restructuring.

433
00:23:05,040 --> 00:23:08,720
If your company was laying you off,

434
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:10,520
would you still say that?

435
00:23:11,920 --> 00:23:13,080
These past two years,

436
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:15,840
top consulting firms worldwide
have been laying off staff.

437
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:18,440
Even the best organizations
need constant elimination and evolution.

438
00:23:19,120 --> 00:23:20,680
No one is irreplaceable.

439
00:23:20,760 --> 00:23:21,680
Not even me.

440
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:25,280
PROMOTE OR QUIT

441
00:23:25,360 --> 00:23:27,880
Wake up. Don't zone out.
Let's hype ourselves up again.

442
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:30,200
We've gotta get this done today.

443
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:31,240
No more hype.

444
00:23:31,320 --> 00:23:33,280
My blood is pure coffee at this point.

445
00:23:33,360 --> 00:23:34,960
It's due tomorrow.

446
00:23:35,040 --> 00:23:36,400
And now the lead has a heart attack.

447
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:38,280
With all this work,
how are we supposed to finish?

448
00:23:38,360 --> 00:23:40,960
Headquarters is sending a big gun
to support us.

449
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:43,600
Morning.

450
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:44,720
Richard!

451
00:23:45,880 --> 00:23:48,320
Hello, everyone. I'm Ye Xinzhi,
sent from headquarters to take over.

452
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:50,040
Who's the project manager here?

453
00:23:50,120 --> 00:23:51,600
Let me see today's summary.

454
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:54,160
Who's that?

455
00:23:54,240 --> 00:23:55,840
You don't know Mr. Ye?

456
00:23:55,920 --> 00:23:58,000
He's the fastest-promoted partner
at C&amp;C Consulting.

457
00:23:58,080 --> 00:24:00,840
He single-handedly closed
the Beihuan Air project.

458
00:24:00,920 --> 00:24:03,080
That impressive?
Then we're saved this time.

459
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:04,080
Everyone,

460
00:24:05,480 --> 00:24:06,840
you've done great work so far.

461
00:24:06,920 --> 00:24:09,560
Now, let's go through
the delivery plan together.

462
00:24:09,640 --> 00:24:10,560
Okay.

463
00:24:11,520 --> 00:24:15,640
Cancel delivery files 003,
007, 013, and 021.

464
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:16,920
Merge 004 and 009.

465
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:19,400
Based on my experience,
with everyone working together,

466
00:24:19,480 --> 00:24:21,720
we can get this done in eight hours.

467
00:24:21,800 --> 00:24:24,200
So here's what I'm assigning.

468
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:25,920
Go back to your rooms
and rest for five hours.

469
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:28,040
But the final delivery meeting
is tomorrow morning!

470
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:30,200
I've already talked to the client.

471
00:24:30,280 --> 00:24:31,600
Pushed it to tomorrow afternoon at four.

472
00:24:32,480 --> 00:24:33,760
Everyone's exhausted.

473
00:24:33,840 --> 00:24:36,160
Without rest, efficiency drops.

474
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:39,160
Amazing.

475
00:24:39,240 --> 00:24:41,520
But I just chugged
two big cans of Red Bull.

476
00:24:41,600 --> 00:24:44,240
My brain is both tired and wired.
I can't sleep at all.

477
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:46,480
I'll figure something out.

478
00:24:57,960 --> 00:25:01,560
<i>Yang Rui, I found some issues</i>
<i>with the Yuanming project.</i>

479
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:05,000
YANG RUI: DATA ERRORS
IN THE YUANMING PROJECT

480
00:25:05,080 --> 00:25:06,240
GO TO THE SITE AND VERIFY NOW

481
00:25:24,440 --> 00:25:25,880
You should go to the restroom
and deal with that.

482
00:25:25,960 --> 00:25:27,000
There's a hairdryer there.

483
00:25:27,080 --> 00:25:29,520
I really didn't know joining Maxmise
meant suffering like this.

484
00:25:29,600 --> 00:25:32,160
I thought the worst would be stuck
at the airport during a typhoon.

485
00:25:32,240 --> 00:25:33,760
Five-thirty in the morning.

486
00:25:33,840 --> 00:25:36,560
My mentor actually wants me
to verify data on-site

487
00:25:36,640 --> 00:25:37,600
-that even the VPA system can't pull.
-Morning.

488
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:38,560
Morning.

489
00:25:40,680 --> 00:25:43,080
Ma'am, she's the first one here again?

490
00:25:43,160 --> 00:25:45,080
Yes. She's first every day.

491
00:25:46,400 --> 00:25:47,600
Crazy.

492
00:25:48,400 --> 00:25:49,560
You don't get it?

493
00:25:49,640 --> 00:25:51,240
That's called scoring points.

494
00:25:52,840 --> 00:25:55,520
I'd love to go to a site
and score points too.

495
00:25:56,400 --> 00:25:58,280
But I don't have that kind of client.

496
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:00,320
My mentor's no help!

497
00:26:02,800 --> 00:26:03,640
It's time for work.

498
00:26:09,360 --> 00:26:11,040
You're really lucky.

499
00:26:11,120 --> 00:26:12,480
You got one who's ready to work.

500
00:26:12,560 --> 00:26:13,960
Jealous?

501
00:26:14,960 --> 00:26:17,280
No wonder Sha Sha
made an exception to hire her.

502
00:26:17,800 --> 00:26:19,160
You know Du Wen's mentee?

503
00:26:19,240 --> 00:26:22,720
Can't even figure out
a simple tool like SPSS.

504
00:26:22,800 --> 00:26:24,320
Gave him a massive headache.

505
00:26:24,400 --> 00:26:26,280
That won't last long, anyway.

506
00:26:26,360 --> 00:26:27,760
Once the three-month probation is over,

507
00:26:27,840 --> 00:26:30,000
at least half these interns will be gone.

508
00:26:32,320 --> 00:26:34,840
Hey, how's Cindy doing?

509
00:26:34,920 --> 00:26:36,080
You sit close to her.

510
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:37,440
Heard anything lately?

511
00:26:39,280 --> 00:26:40,800
You were right.

512
00:26:40,880 --> 00:26:41,760
You know what?

513
00:26:41,840 --> 00:26:45,400
Cindy invited Mr. Zheng from Dongfang Data
to play golf and have dinner.

514
00:26:45,480 --> 00:26:46,960
She asked Bu Tianna to join them at night.

515
00:26:47,040 --> 00:26:48,560
You know what Bu Tianna said?

516
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:52,440
"I already have plans tonight."

517
00:26:52,520 --> 00:26:54,320
Before Cindy could even react,

518
00:26:54,400 --> 00:26:56,560
Mr. Zheng called and canceled the dinner.

519
00:26:58,480 --> 00:27:00,800
She thought she'd scored a gem.

520
00:27:00,880 --> 00:27:01,760
And then?

521
00:27:02,280 --> 00:27:03,680
She just has to take the loss.

522
00:27:03,760 --> 00:27:05,720
If you want to move up, you pay the price.

523
00:27:06,760 --> 00:27:08,120
Don't forget Maxmise's rule.

524
00:27:10,360 --> 00:27:12,200
-Get promoted or get out.
-Get promoted or get out.

525
00:27:12,760 --> 00:27:14,360
Come on. Let's toast.

526
00:27:31,040 --> 00:27:33,160
-Morning.
-Morning.

527
00:27:34,480 --> 00:27:35,760
Just graduated and already looking
to buy an apartment?

528
00:27:35,840 --> 00:27:37,320
Pretty ambitious for a young person.

529
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:38,680
Gotta make good money.

530
00:27:40,120 --> 00:27:42,080
The agent sent it to me.
I was just browsing.

531
00:27:43,200 --> 00:27:45,560
-What proposal are you working on?
-The proposal of Bolo Culture.

532
00:27:45,640 --> 00:27:47,280
Once Ms. Lin reviews it,
I'll send it over to you.

533
00:27:56,680 --> 00:27:57,680
Clean work.

534
00:27:58,600 --> 00:28:02,080
Lin Long has been praising you
a lot these days.

535
00:28:02,160 --> 00:28:03,240
By the way, where do you live?

536
00:28:03,320 --> 00:28:05,480
How do you get to the office
so early every day?

537
00:28:06,520 --> 00:28:08,320
Just around the corner
at the diplomatic compound--

538
00:28:08,400 --> 00:28:09,360
Diplomatic compound?

539
00:28:09,440 --> 00:28:11,080
That's not cheap, is it?

540
00:28:11,160 --> 00:28:14,160
There's a 9 Days Inn nearby.
I've rented a standard room long-term.

541
00:28:14,680 --> 00:28:16,560
A standard room at 9 Days Inn?

542
00:28:16,640 --> 00:28:20,000
That's probably just a bed and a bathroom.
So small.

543
00:28:20,080 --> 00:28:22,560
It's fine. Enough for me.

544
00:28:22,640 --> 00:28:24,440
Bigger than my dorm room.

545
00:28:24,520 --> 00:28:27,360
It's slightly more expensive
than a studio,

546
00:28:27,440 --> 00:28:31,040
but I'll be working
at least ten hours a day

547
00:28:31,120 --> 00:28:32,960
and traveling at least
eight times a month.

548
00:28:33,040 --> 00:28:35,320
Compared to a landlord
who might kick me out anytime,

549
00:28:35,400 --> 00:28:38,320
a hotel with 24/7 hot water and Wi-Fi
suits me much better.

550
00:28:38,960 --> 00:28:39,800
Why push yourself so hard?

551
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:43,880
If I didn't, you wouldn't have noticed me

552
00:28:43,960 --> 00:28:45,680
or asked me that question.

553
00:28:47,720 --> 00:28:50,160
After you read my report,
if you think it's decent,

554
00:28:50,680 --> 00:28:53,280
can I join Ms. Lin
for the proposal meeting?

555
00:28:54,520 --> 00:28:56,760
We have no precedent
for interns joining proposal meetings.

556
00:28:57,560 --> 00:28:59,440
I'll prove with my report

557
00:28:59,520 --> 00:29:01,480
that I'm already
at a full-time employee's level.

558
00:29:05,800 --> 00:29:08,760
Our project proposal
is in the final stage.

559
00:29:09,880 --> 00:29:11,760
Yang Rui's team is swamped anyway.

560
00:29:11,840 --> 00:29:13,640
Since on-site inspection is so important,

561
00:29:13,720 --> 00:29:15,400
why not send Bu Tianna
to get some experience?

562
00:29:15,480 --> 00:29:17,120
You think she doesn't
listen to you enough,

563
00:29:17,200 --> 00:29:18,800
so you want to knock her down
a peg, don't you?

564
00:29:19,680 --> 00:29:21,760
Cindy, as a mentor,

565
00:29:21,840 --> 00:29:23,800
you should have a broader mindset.

566
00:29:23,880 --> 00:29:25,920
Tianna is still a fine blade
that needs sharpening.

567
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:28,720
But you can't dull her
on a construction site.

568
00:29:30,960 --> 00:29:33,160
I read the Bolo Culture documents.
Not bad.

569
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:35,480
Just a bit conservative in style.

570
00:29:35,560 --> 00:29:37,800
Why don't you bring Xu Chi
to the proposal meeting this time?

571
00:29:37,880 --> 00:29:38,840
She's young.

572
00:29:38,920 --> 00:29:41,400
Perfect for her to connect
with those new unicorn startup folks.

573
00:29:43,120 --> 00:29:44,640
The industry summit organized
by the Research

574
00:29:44,720 --> 00:29:45,560
is coming up in a couple of days.

575
00:29:45,640 --> 00:29:47,640
Mr. Pi said we should go help out.

576
00:29:48,560 --> 00:29:49,440
Okay.

577
00:29:49,960 --> 00:29:51,480
In our team…

578
00:29:54,280 --> 00:29:55,960
-I'll get to work then.
-Go ahead.

579
00:30:00,520 --> 00:30:01,920
Need a reminder?

580
00:30:03,240 --> 00:30:05,160
The surname Bu isn't common.

581
00:30:08,840 --> 00:30:10,000
Remember now?

582
00:30:10,800 --> 00:30:12,960
You usually seem pretty sharp.

583
00:30:13,040 --> 00:30:14,320
How'd you get so dense this time?

584
00:30:17,000 --> 00:30:18,280
Guess that's why we're friends.

585
00:30:18,360 --> 00:30:20,440
Even you got fooled by Xu Chi.
My situation is nothing.

586
00:30:22,200 --> 00:30:24,840
You know why Sha Sha asked you
to bring Xu Chi to the proposal meeting?

587
00:30:25,840 --> 00:30:27,120
This morning…

588
00:30:29,680 --> 00:30:32,120
<i>Lin Long has been praising you</i>
<i>a lot these days.</i>

589
00:30:32,720 --> 00:30:35,240
Can I join Ms. Lin
for the proposal meeting?

590
00:30:38,680 --> 00:30:40,280
<i>Lately, you've been leaving before eight.</i>

591
00:30:40,360 --> 00:30:41,800
<i>Xu Chi handles most of the work now.</i>

592
00:30:41,880 --> 00:30:43,120
<i>Feels pretty easy?</i>

593
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:46,160
Ms. Lin, you're pregnant.
You shouldn't overdo it.

594
00:30:46,240 --> 00:30:48,360
Why don't you head home?
I'll handle the rest.

595
00:30:48,960 --> 00:30:49,720
Thank you.

596
00:30:51,120 --> 00:30:53,400
Jealous? You're really lucky.

597
00:30:53,480 --> 00:30:55,080
You got one who's ready to work.

598
00:30:55,720 --> 00:30:58,720
You really don't know why
Yang Rui's team is so swamped?

599
00:30:58,800 --> 00:31:01,680
Because Xu Chi has sharp eyes.

600
00:31:08,160 --> 00:31:10,760
<i>She spotted a data error he missed.</i>

601
00:31:10,840 --> 00:31:13,400
And she sent the email
under your team's name.

602
00:31:13,480 --> 00:31:15,960
Since the Yuanming project
is a collaboration with Yang Rui's team,

603
00:31:16,040 --> 00:31:18,480
can I just communicate with them directly?

604
00:31:18,560 --> 00:31:20,720
Sure. On this project,
we're the front end.

605
00:31:20,800 --> 00:31:21,640
They're the back end.

606
00:31:24,560 --> 00:31:26,520
She embarrassed him.

607
00:31:26,600 --> 00:31:27,440
YANG RUI

608
00:31:27,520 --> 00:31:28,880
<i>Data errors found in the Yuanming project.</i>

609
00:31:28,960 --> 00:31:30,600
<i>Go to the site and verify now.</i>

610
00:31:31,280 --> 00:31:33,120
Sorry, Yang Rui. I'm on my way.

611
00:31:33,200 --> 00:31:34,440
I'll verify the data on-site right away.

612
00:31:34,520 --> 00:31:36,120
I'll have it done before work starts.

613
00:31:36,200 --> 00:31:39,320
<i>Deng Anran was forced to go to the site</i>
<i>and recheck every single piece of data.</i>

614
00:31:41,520 --> 00:31:44,120
You forgot what happened between them
when they first joined?

615
00:31:44,200 --> 00:31:45,160
You don't even have an English name?

616
00:31:45,920 --> 00:31:47,080
Not answering directly?

617
00:31:47,160 --> 00:31:49,520
Guess your school and name
aren't worth mentioning.

618
00:31:49,600 --> 00:31:52,760
You've been used as a pawn.

619
00:31:53,360 --> 00:31:54,440
No way.

620
00:31:55,080 --> 00:31:56,720
Why not?

621
00:31:57,600 --> 00:31:59,160
You thought she was a pushover.

622
00:31:59,240 --> 00:32:02,360
She waited until everyone forgot,
then got her revenge.

623
00:32:02,440 --> 00:32:04,480
She is more calculating than you.

624
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:07,920
Now she's bypassed you and gone
straight to Sha Sha for the proposal.

625
00:32:08,520 --> 00:32:12,120
By the time you're back,
your spot will be gone.

626
00:32:12,200 --> 00:32:14,160
And you thought you'd found a gem.

627
00:32:26,680 --> 00:32:29,440
Zhao Heng. Do you know where Xu Chi went?

628
00:32:29,520 --> 00:32:31,520
She's in Meeting Room B, meeting visitors.

629
00:32:32,240 --> 00:32:33,360
Visitors?

630
00:32:34,800 --> 00:32:36,560
You mean e-commerce formation?

631
00:32:36,640 --> 00:32:39,360
Yes. Our strategy
actually serves the national priorities,

632
00:32:39,440 --> 00:32:41,200
rural revitalization, healthcare,
emergency response,

633
00:32:41,280 --> 00:32:42,280
and down-market e-commerce.

634
00:32:42,360 --> 00:32:43,400
Xu Chi.

635
00:32:44,560 --> 00:32:45,640
Step out for a moment.

636
00:32:47,120 --> 00:32:48,080
One second, please.

637
00:32:52,480 --> 00:32:53,480
What's up, Ms. Lin?

638
00:32:54,800 --> 00:32:55,760
Who are those people?

639
00:32:57,480 --> 00:32:59,680
They're from the Beijing Low-Altitude
Economy Industry Research Institute.

640
00:32:59,760 --> 00:33:03,000
The Yuanming drone logistics project
has some policy issues,

641
00:33:03,080 --> 00:33:04,440
so I invited them over for a workshop.

642
00:33:04,520 --> 00:33:06,000
I asked you about it yesterday.

643
00:33:06,080 --> 00:33:08,360
I said we could consider it.
I didn't say to do it right away.

644
00:33:08,440 --> 00:33:10,640
What are their titles?
How credible are they?

645
00:33:10,720 --> 00:33:13,320
You just grab any random people
and call it a workshop?

646
00:33:13,400 --> 00:33:14,800
Trying to cash in on Maxmise's name?

647
00:33:14,880 --> 00:33:17,720
And did you apply for a budget
for their appearance fees?

648
00:33:17,800 --> 00:33:21,880
Xu Chi, do you think just because
I've been praising you lately,

649
00:33:21,960 --> 00:33:24,080
you can get cocky and make your own calls?

650
00:33:28,200 --> 00:33:30,960
The one at the far end
is Deputy Director Zheng.

651
00:33:31,040 --> 00:33:32,280
Next to him is Section Chief Song,

652
00:33:32,360 --> 00:33:33,600
who oversees the low-altitude economy
in the district.

653
00:33:34,280 --> 00:33:35,920
This workshop doesn't need a budget.

654
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:37,280
I traded a free share of Maxmise's

655
00:33:37,360 --> 00:33:39,360
Southeast Asia logistics industry report
for it.

656
00:33:39,440 --> 00:33:41,880
Also, I was able
to get them here so quickly

657
00:33:41,960 --> 00:33:44,920
because I once did
a winter break internship

658
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:46,360
at Mr. Zheng's Tiandi Logistics.

659
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:47,920
He's always had a good impression of me.

660
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:49,080
Even so,

661
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:50,880
who said you could share
our report for free?

662
00:33:54,560 --> 00:33:56,520
Xu Chi, your delivery is here.

663
00:33:56,600 --> 00:33:57,960
Great. Thanks.

664
00:33:58,560 --> 00:34:00,160
Let me finish the meeting first.
I'll talk to you after.

665
00:34:01,120 --> 00:34:02,680
Sorry for the wait.

666
00:34:03,200 --> 00:34:04,240
-Mr. Zheng.
-Well, well.

667
00:34:04,320 --> 00:34:06,040
This is your favorite oat latte.

668
00:34:06,800 --> 00:34:07,720
Thank you.

669
00:34:08,320 --> 00:34:11,520
-And Mr. Song's Americano.
-Thanks.

670
00:34:12,600 --> 00:34:14,040
-Over here.
-Alright, Xu.

671
00:34:14,120 --> 00:34:15,440
-We'll catch up next time.
-Alright.

672
00:34:16,639 --> 00:34:19,600
Xu, keep me posted
on the project progress.

673
00:34:19,679 --> 00:34:20,520
I will, Mr. Song. Thank you.

674
00:34:20,600 --> 00:34:21,639
-See you.
-Bye.

675
00:34:21,719 --> 00:34:22,639
Take care.

676
00:34:26,080 --> 00:34:27,239
Xu Chi.

677
00:34:29,880 --> 00:34:31,040
Lin Long stepped out.

678
00:34:31,120 --> 00:34:32,159
She told me

679
00:34:32,239 --> 00:34:34,320
you don't need to attend the Bolo Culture
workshop this afternoon.

680
00:34:34,920 --> 00:34:37,040
The Research is hosting
an industry summit at Dongfang Hotel.

681
00:34:37,120 --> 00:34:39,080
They're short-handed
on the Conference Team.

682
00:34:39,159 --> 00:34:40,120
She wants you to go help out there.

683
00:34:42,760 --> 00:34:44,040
Got it. Thanks.

684
00:34:45,960 --> 00:34:49,800
Are you getting pushed back
because you performed too well?

685
00:34:52,400 --> 00:34:53,239
So what?

686
00:34:53,840 --> 00:34:55,480
It was made clear on day one.

687
00:34:55,560 --> 00:34:57,040
Mentors are just mentors.

688
00:34:57,120 --> 00:35:00,640
Whether an intern stays
is ultimately Sha Sha's call.

689
00:35:00,720 --> 00:35:02,920
As long as I stay at Maxmise,
a couple of years from now,

690
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:04,400
tables could turn.

691
00:35:06,960 --> 00:35:10,360
I'm glad someone else gets that too.

692
00:35:20,920 --> 00:35:22,120
It's heavy. Easy.

693
00:35:22,200 --> 00:35:23,280
Over here.

694
00:35:23,360 --> 00:35:27,120
This is the additional venue setup
as you requested.

695
00:35:28,760 --> 00:35:30,040
Take care.

696
00:35:30,120 --> 00:35:31,000
Excuse me.

697
00:35:34,560 --> 00:35:35,400
Mr. Pi?

698
00:35:37,640 --> 00:35:39,440
-Mr. Pi?
-Go on.

699
00:35:39,520 --> 00:35:41,160
The halal and vegan options

700
00:35:41,240 --> 00:35:44,120
you requested for the lunch guests
have all been taken care of.

701
00:35:44,200 --> 00:35:45,040
Got it.

702
00:35:57,720 --> 00:35:59,920
You sent Xu Chi to do grunt work?

703
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:03,160
If you want to knock her down,
at least don't make it so obvious.

704
00:36:03,240 --> 00:36:05,480
I'm telling you, Mr. Pi knows.

705
00:36:06,120 --> 00:36:07,160
So what?

706
00:36:07,240 --> 00:36:08,680
Deng Anran got sent
to a construction site.

707
00:36:08,760 --> 00:36:10,760
Can't Xu Chi go to a hotel to help out?

708
00:36:12,120 --> 00:36:13,880
Let me tell you some real tea.

709
00:36:13,960 --> 00:36:15,440
You don't know she's from
a non-elite school, do you?

710
00:36:17,400 --> 00:36:20,640
I only knew she didn't study abroad
and that she's not from a top school.

711
00:36:20,720 --> 00:36:22,360
How did someone not from a top school
get into Maxmise?

712
00:36:23,600 --> 00:36:24,440
You…

713
00:36:24,520 --> 00:36:26,160
Sit, sit. Have a seat.

714
00:36:26,240 --> 00:36:27,600
What are you doing?

715
00:36:28,960 --> 00:36:31,200
Because she and the SJTU team

716
00:36:31,280 --> 00:36:34,200
won first place in Beisen's
Yangfan Cup business competition.

717
00:36:36,800 --> 00:36:39,800
<i>Her champion title</i>
<i>was judged by Mr. Pi himself.</i>

718
00:36:40,880 --> 00:36:42,920
She was actually planning to go to Beisen,

719
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:46,640
but you know, Beisen moved
its headquarters to Shenzhen this year,

720
00:36:46,720 --> 00:36:47,760
so she hesitated.

721
00:36:48,360 --> 00:36:49,440
When Mr. Pi found out,

722
00:36:49,520 --> 00:36:51,640
he sent her an offer right away.

723
00:36:51,720 --> 00:36:54,800
You know what her GPA is?

724
00:36:54,880 --> 00:36:56,720
3.95.

725
00:36:57,440 --> 00:36:59,440
Last night after midnight,

726
00:36:59,520 --> 00:37:00,800
Mr. Pi came to the office
to grab some files

727
00:37:00,880 --> 00:37:04,200
and heard about Xu Chi's workshop plan.

728
00:37:04,280 --> 00:37:05,560
He read it and was impressed.

729
00:37:05,640 --> 00:37:08,280
He approved her sharing the report
for free on the spot.

730
00:37:08,360 --> 00:37:11,400
And then you turned around
and sent her to do grunt work.

731
00:37:11,480 --> 00:37:13,280
Aren't you basically
slapping Mr. Pi in the face?

732
00:37:13,800 --> 00:37:14,880
Even so,

733
00:37:14,960 --> 00:37:16,680
who said you could share
our report for free?

734
00:37:20,280 --> 00:37:22,800
Just now, Mr. Pi called the
Conference Team

735
00:37:22,880 --> 00:37:26,440
and asked why they pulled
a project colleague to do errands.

736
00:37:30,520 --> 00:37:33,800
You know how fierce the competition is
in consulting right now.

737
00:37:34,400 --> 00:37:37,240
Xu Chi is clearly someone
who can really get things done.

738
00:37:37,320 --> 00:37:39,400
If you piss off Mr. Pi because of her,

739
00:37:39,480 --> 00:37:42,640
aren't you afraid
he'll give you a hard time at work?

740
00:37:49,080 --> 00:37:50,800
Think about what you're going to do.
I've got work.

741
00:38:09,760 --> 00:38:10,640
<i>Xu Chi.</i>

742
00:38:10,720 --> 00:38:12,600
<i>Come back after you pick up</i>
<i>the guest at the airport.</i>

743
00:38:12,680 --> 00:38:14,440
<i>Mr. Pi chewed us out because of you.</i>

744
00:38:14,520 --> 00:38:16,680
<i>Oh, did you get the pickup sign?</i>

745
00:38:16,760 --> 00:38:19,240
I already got it. Don't worry.

746
00:38:25,080 --> 00:38:26,920
<i>I will never be replaced by anyone.</i>

747
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:30,080
<i>I'll be the one to push out</i>
<i>those competing with me first.</i>

748
00:38:33,120 --> 00:38:34,480
XU CHI

749
00:38:34,560 --> 00:38:35,760
<i>Thanks.</i>

750
00:38:35,840 --> 00:38:37,040
<i>You're welcome.</i>

751
00:38:37,120 --> 00:38:40,480
<i>I just told the lobby manager</i>
<i>at Dongfang Hotel</i>

752
00:38:40,560 --> 00:38:42,360
<i>to ask Mr. Pi to step out for a chat.</i>

753
00:38:42,440 --> 00:38:44,200
XU CHI, BU TIANNA

754
00:38:44,280 --> 00:38:45,240
<i>Why do you keep helping me?</i>

755
00:38:46,120 --> 00:38:48,960
<i>I'm going to become a partner someday.</i>

756
00:38:49,040 --> 00:38:51,520
<i>I just want to start building</i>
<i>my inner circle early.</i>

757
00:38:54,560 --> 00:38:56,240
<i>Too bad that when I play chess,</i>

758
00:38:56,320 --> 00:38:58,000
<i>I'm not good at being a knight.</i>

759
00:38:58,600 --> 00:38:59,760
<i>I'm only good at being the queen.</i>

760
00:39:00,280 --> 00:39:01,360
Really?

761
00:39:13,080 --> 00:39:15,200
The Beihuan Air project is done.

762
00:39:15,280 --> 00:39:17,360
This time I'm here for the Tianhe project.

763
00:39:18,480 --> 00:39:21,560
Right, send me the data again
so I can take a look.

764
00:39:24,240 --> 00:39:25,200
Okay.

765
00:39:37,960 --> 00:39:40,400
Mr. Yi, we'll be at the hotel
in half an hour.

766
00:39:40,480 --> 00:39:42,480
Your room service order
for the Caesar salad is on its way.

767
00:39:43,080 --> 00:39:44,360
I hate Caesar salad.

768
00:39:49,800 --> 00:39:51,200
Did you pick up the wrong person?

769
00:39:53,160 --> 00:39:54,120
Sir, please pull over.

770
00:39:54,200 --> 00:39:55,080
Sure.

771
00:39:57,520 --> 00:39:58,640
RICHARD YE, DONGFANG HOTEL

772
00:39:59,920 --> 00:40:00,960
Sorry.

773
00:40:05,920 --> 00:40:08,880
Mr. Yi, I'm from Maxmise,
who texted you earlier to pick you up.

774
00:40:10,160 --> 00:40:11,720
Still waiting for your luggage?
No worries. Take your time.

775
00:40:11,800 --> 00:40:13,960
I'll take a lap around the other floors.

776
00:40:14,560 --> 00:40:15,680
Okay. I'll wait for your call.

777
00:40:18,280 --> 00:40:20,680
Mr. Ye, I'm sorry. I didn't double-check
the name on the pickup sign.

778
00:40:20,760 --> 00:40:22,760
I have two temporary solutions.

779
00:40:22,840 --> 00:40:24,160
One, I can take you back to the airport.

780
00:40:24,240 --> 00:40:25,880
Two, if you're in a hurry,

781
00:40:25,960 --> 00:40:27,040
I'll have the driver
take you to the hotel,

782
00:40:27,120 --> 00:40:29,080
and then I'll get off
and order another car for Mr. Yi.

783
00:40:29,160 --> 00:40:30,480
Which option works better for you?

784
00:40:31,160 --> 00:40:32,200
One.

785
00:40:33,800 --> 00:40:35,000
Please drive back to the airport.
And hurry.

786
00:40:35,600 --> 00:40:37,200
-Alright.
-You remember me?

787
00:40:39,400 --> 00:40:40,240
Of course.

788
00:40:41,720 --> 00:40:43,680
Admitted the mistake cleanly.
Didn't pass the buck.

789
00:40:43,760 --> 00:40:46,080
Quickly offered solutions
for the client to choose from.

790
00:40:47,920 --> 00:40:49,360
You do look like a consultant now.

791
00:40:51,680 --> 00:40:53,440
Congratulations. Your wish came true.

792
00:40:55,800 --> 00:40:56,800
Thanks.

793
00:40:57,400 --> 00:40:59,400
What's wrong? Not going well?

794
00:41:00,400 --> 00:41:01,360
That's not it.

795
00:41:03,480 --> 00:41:04,720
Never mind then.

796
00:41:24,160 --> 00:41:25,360
Bye, Mr. Yi.

797
00:41:35,520 --> 00:41:36,360
Mr. Ye.

798
00:41:36,440 --> 00:41:37,360
-Long time no see.
-Long time no see.

799
00:41:37,440 --> 00:41:38,560
-Everything going well?
-Yes.

800
00:41:39,160 --> 00:41:41,400
-Come on. Your room is all set.
-Alright. Let's go.

801
00:41:43,120 --> 00:41:45,160
Wang Yu's hosting a welcome dinner
for you tonight.

802
00:41:45,240 --> 00:41:46,640
-Great.
-We'll have a little drink.

803
00:41:49,160 --> 00:41:50,360
SEARCHING FOR YE XINZHI

804
00:41:50,440 --> 00:41:51,960
YE XINZHI'S PROFILE

805
00:41:52,040 --> 00:41:54,240
2017-2022: ASSOCIATE PARTNER
EY HEYI CONSULTING

806
00:41:54,320 --> 00:41:56,800
2022-2023: OPERATIONS GM, P&amp;J

807
00:41:56,880 --> 00:41:58,640
2023: CMO, ANDE ENERGY

808
00:41:58,720 --> 00:42:02,440
2023-PRESENT: GLOBAL MANAGING PARTNER
C&amp;C CONSULTING

809
00:42:03,800 --> 00:42:05,840
I've finished the revisions.
I'll email it to you in a bit.

810
00:42:06,840 --> 00:42:07,680
Bye.

811
00:42:11,040 --> 00:42:12,400
Sir, your package.

812
00:42:12,480 --> 00:42:13,440
Thanks.

813
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:25,600
APOLOGIES AGAIN, AND THANK YOU.
XU CHI
